    <edge source="People" target="Driving">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Individuals are advised not to engage in driving until medical mechanisms are ascertained and standards are met.</data>
      <data key="d9">restriction,safety</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-05643c50d6cf5973-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-05643c50d6cf5973</data>
      <data key="d12">1792686770</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vasovagal Syncope" target="Driving">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The condition of vasovagal syncope may require an assessment of fitness to drive depending on the cause and likelihood of recurrence.</data>
      <data key="d9">fitness assessment,provoking factors,restrictions</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-BLK-COM-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-BLK-COM-002</data>
      <data key="d12">1792686731</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vasovagal Syncope" target="Cardiovascular Conditions Standards">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">When vasovagal syncope arises from causes other than benign provoking factors, the assessment of fitness to drive follows the cardiovascular conditions standards.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment criteria,non-benign causes</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-BLK-COM-002-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-BLK-COM-002</data>
      <data key="d12">1792686731</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vasovagal Syncope" target="Blackout">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Vasovagal syncope is a primary cause of blackouts, accounting for more than 50 per cent of cases.</data>
      <data key="d9">cause,mechanism,percentage</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-fc1ed73935da2203-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-fc1ed73935da2203</data>
      <data key="d12">1792686856</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Person" target="Unconditional Licence">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A person is determined to be unfit for holding an unconditional licence based on specific medical or diagnostic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A person is not fit to hold an unconditional licence if they have experienced blackouts that cannot be diagnosed as syncope, seizure, or another condition.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,eligibility,fitness,fitness to drive</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-BLK-COM-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-BLK-COM-004-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-BLK-COM-003&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-BLK-COM-004</data>
      <data key="d12">1792686745</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Person" target="Blackout of Undetermined Nature">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A person is prohibited from driving for ten years if they experience two or more blackouts of undetermined nature separated by a 24-hour period.&lt;SEP&gt;A person is prohibited from driving for five years after experiencing a single blackout of undetermined nature.</data>
      <data key="d9">driving restriction,medical history</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-BLK-COM-004-chunk-000</data>
